    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d946">

                <pb facs="0733" n="617" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg617"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13649.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Canova to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aguascalientes</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-02T13:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 2, 1914, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At midnight the Convention declared General Eulalio Gutiérrez. Governor of the
                    State of San Luis Potosí, elected Provisional President of the Republic of
                    Mexico. The Zapatistas declared themselves perfectly satisfied and avowed their
                    allegiance to the President-elect.</p>
                <p>General Gutiérrez is elected for a period of twenty days, when the Convention,
                    with a full attendance of thirty authorized Zapata delegates, will ratify his
                    permanency as Provisional President until his duly elected successor can assume
                    office or another be named to fill out the provisional term.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canova</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
